<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3567" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκρό-κομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμη</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with hair on crown</i>, epith. of Thracians, who
			either tied up their hair in a top-knot, or shaved all their head
			except crown, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.533
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				1.4
			</span></i>; <i>with hair at tip</i>, of goat's chin, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				34.10.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>with leafy crown</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1516
			</span></i>; esp. of palms, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				2.53
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.P.
				1010
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κυπάρισσοι</span>
			<i>tapering</i> cypresses, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.41
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>